# The program's own type test before a branch replaces the check after the read. The test covers the full type, and on its failing edge a check covers the rest of the proven type.
# The injected fault treats what the program passes to unknown code as non-escaping. Link does not see the store made by the evaluated source, and keeps claiming what the array held at first.
# RUN: run-in-shell mechanisms=all
# CHECK: text
# CHECK-NEXT: nothing
# CHECK-NEXT: went on
# CHECK-NEXT: exited with 0
# RUN(SHAPE): walk f1 mechanisms=all testing=AssumeArgumentsNeverEscape
# SHAPE: CheckProof {{*}}source=Contents [isLeftToTestBehind]
# SHAPE: TypeTest {{*}}[asksInFull]
# SHAPE: CheckProof {{*}}source=Contents
# RUN(FAULT): run-in-shell mechanisms=all testing=AssumeArgumentsNeverEscape
# FAULT: text
# FAULT: found int32 in an element
# FAULT-NOT: went on
# FAULT: crashed
